      "message": "Thanks for the detail info.\n\nMy device was\n```\nOcta-core (2x2.85 GHz Cortex-X1 \u0026 2x2.35 GHz Cortex-A78 \u0026 4x1.80 GHz Cortex-A55)\n```\n\nI ran it on little/middle/big core affinity.\n\nAnyway, the put_page overhead would be higher than other function in pinner.h\n\nThen, this patch fixes your regression?\n\n```\n static inline void page_pinner_failure_detect(struct page *page)\n {\n-       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026failure_tracking))\n+       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026page_pinner_inited))\n                return;\n-\n        __page_pinner_migration_failed(page);\n }\n \n static inline void page_pinner_mark_migration_failed_pages(struct list_head *page_list)\n {\n-       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026failure_tracking))\n+       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026page_pinner_inited))\n                return;\n-\n        __page_pinner_mark_migration_failed_pages(page_list);\n }\n #else\ndiff --git a/mm/page_pinner.c b/mm/page_pinner.c\nindex a444584103ad..738c4c219ba7 100644\n--- a/mm/page_pinner.c\n+++ b/mm/page_pinner.c\n@@ -337,6 +337,9 @@ void __page_pinner_migration_failed(struct page *page)\n        unsigned long flags;\n        unsigned int idx;\n \n+       if (!static_branch_unlikely(\u0026failure_tracking))\n+               return;\n+\n        if (unlikely(!page_ext))\n                return;\n\n```",
